<title>USA: Ground Round sees weaker Q3 earnings.</title>
<headline>Ground Round sees weaker Q3 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>BRAINTREE, Mass. 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ground Round Restaurants Inc said Wednesday it expects lower-than-expected quarterly earnings.</p>
<p>The restaurant said both earnings and cash flow for the third quarter ended June 30, 1997 should fall lower than expected, but gave no specifics, as June revenues fell 6.3 percent.  It said the sales trend continued into the first two weeks of July 1997.</p>
<p>Ground Round shares closed at $2 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The company posted a loss of $0.28 a share in the year-ago third quarter.</p>
</text>
